response:
Here's an implementation of bubble sort in C++ for sorting an integer array:

```cpp
void bubbleSort(int arr[], int n) {
    bool swapped = true; // flag to keep track of any swaps during a pass
    int end = n-1; // index of last element

    // iterate through all elements until no swaps are made
    while (swapped) {
        swapped = false; // reset flag for current pass

        // iterate through array from first to second last element
        for (int i=0; i<=end-1; ++i) {
            if (arr[i] > arr[i+1]) { // swap adjacent elements if they are in wrong order
                int temp = arr[i];
                arr[i] = arr[i+1];
                arr[i+1] = temp;
                swapped = true; // set flag if any swaps were made during this iteration
            }
        }

        --end; // decrement end index for next pass
    }
}
```

