```js
function generateNotificationMessage(notifObj) {
  let weightedRating = 0;
  let bestNotification = null;

  for (const [notifType, notifArr] of Object.entries(notifObj)) {
    let helpfulness = 0;
    let verbosity = 0;

    // Calculate helpfulness and verbosity scores for each notification in this type
    for (const notification of notifArr) {
      helpfulness += notification.helpfulness;
      verbosity += notification.text.length;
    }

    // Calculate weighted rating for this notification type
    const weightedRatingType = helpfulness * 91 + verbosity * 42;

    // Check if this is the best notification type so far
    if (!bestNotification || weightedRatingType > weightedRating) {
      weightedRating = weightedRatingType;
      bestNotification = {
        notifType,
        message: notifArr[0].message
      };
    }
  }

  return bestNotification;
}
```

This function takes an object `notifObj` where keys are notification types and values are arrays of notifications with properties `helpfulness` and `text`. It calculates the weighted rating for each notification type using the formula `helpfulness * 91 + verbosity * 42`, where `helpfulness` represents the helpfulness score and `verbosity` represents the length of the text message. The function returns an object containing the best notification type found along with its corresponding message.

